WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.147
The mini-project asks you to apply the full workflow rather than only repeat individual code cells.

00:00:07.147 --> 00:00:10.272
Use at least eight source documents.

00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:17.422
Preserve useful metadata. Chunk the documents, create embeddings, build dense retrieval, add a metadata filter,

00:00:17.422 --> 00:00:22.387
and create a grounded prompt with citations.

00:00:22.387 --> 00:00:27.282
Then build a small evaluation set with at least eight questions.

00:00:27.282 --> 00:00:34.892
Your project should show the evidence path from source document to chunk to retrieved result to final answer.

00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:40.324
For an optional extension, move the vectors into Chroma, Qdrant, or FAISS.

00:00:40.324 --> 00:00:46.004
You can also add BM25, hybrid retrieval, reranking, or a Streamlit interface.

00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:50.819
The goal is not to include the largest number of features.

00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:56.559
The goal is to demonstrate that you understand the architecture, can inspect retrieval,

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:02.736
and can explain why the final answer is supported by the retrieved evidence.
